WEBVTT

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.080
I am Reinbach Jamil,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:24.450
Reinhart's father and the previous duke.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.700
Pleased to meet you.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.450
R-Right.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:37.580
I'm Elise Jamil, Reinhart's wife.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.830
Thank you for saving my husband
and his men the other day.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.000
You're welcome.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.000
This is our daughter, Eliaria.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.410
I am Eliaria Jamil.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.330
Nice to meet you.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.080
Um...

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.540
Oh, um, nice to meet you.
I am Ryoma Takebayashi.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.910
Thank you for coming all the way out here!

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.580
I apologize for not being able to
offer any proper hospitality...

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.290
There's no need for that.
It's our fault for arriving unannounced.

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:16.950
I heard you had made contracts with many slimes,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.500
but I didn't expect <i>this </i>many.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.950
Is it just me, or have they grown in number?

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.870
They've split since then.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.040
Can they fit in your house?

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.870
They've learned how to.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:30.620
Learned?

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.330
Like this.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.040
Everyone, join up!

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:17.950
"Episode 2"
"Departure, with the Slimes"

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:27.330
As you see, a group of over 100 slimes
of the same type can combine.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:31.040
They can also use a skill called "minimize,"

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.450
which allows me to conserve space and food...

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.120
U-Uh...

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.950
A big slime?!

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.620
Incredible!

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.870
Y-You tamed a big slime?!

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.080
Huh?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:53.000
Nobody has ever successfully
tamed a big slime before!

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.000
Huh?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.080
The Taming Contract has no effect on them!
I've never heard of this succeeding!

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.160
Oh, well, um, the big slimes...

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.370
It does appear like they only have one core,

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.910
but it's actually over 100 cores
joined together.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:12.700
Entering into a contract with 100 monsters
at the same time is impossible.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:18.370
In my case, I first tamed 100 separate slimes,
and then joined them, so...

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.160
Amazing...!

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.040
Incredible!

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:26.660
You've solved the mystery
that every tamer has faced!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.040
Wh-What?!

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.250
Madam.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:34.000
Please calm down. You are scaring Mr. Ryoma.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.790
Oh! I'm sorry!

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.700
It's fine.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:44.620
B-But really, just taming more than
100 slimes is impressive just by itself.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:48.500
Yes. I never thought I'd see

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:52.330
the answer to this mystery in my lifetime.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:56.370
You should register with
the Tamers' Guild and present this!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.000
Tamers' Guild?

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.660
Oh, right, there's an organization
that collects that type of info.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.370
Well, um...

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:07.040
I don't want to make you
stay standing. Please come in.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.250
Yes, thank you.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.160
Get small!

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.160
So.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:24.540
We were slightly... or rather, very surprised
and almost forgot why we came.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:28.330
Ryoma, please take this as a token of
our gratitude for the other day.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.870
What an impressive clock!

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:35.120
I don't mean to insult you,
but we noticed you didn't own a clock.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.290
But...

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:39.040
Don't worry about it, just take it.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:43.540
Given all you did for us,
it's almost not enough.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.250
It's not like you got it for him, you know.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.200
Well, yeah, but...

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:52.000
Thank you very much. I will accept.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.500
I will treasure this.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.040
Good.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.120
There is another reason why
we came to the forest.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.330
Reason?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.750
W-We, the Jamil family, are a family of tamers!

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:12.950
I've come to tame my first familiar,
and would like to catch a slime!

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:15.790
Ah, I see.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.540
So, did you find a slime...?

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:20.700
We couldn't find any on our way here.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:23.540
I see. Then...

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.250
Slimes often come to this area to drink water.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:33.040
I'd like to go there.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:35.500
Mr. Ryoma!

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:36.660
Yes?

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.660
I'm still not sure what type
of slime I should capture.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:44.410
The sticky slime, acid slime, poison slime,

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.910
and healing slime were in some books.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:50.950
But the two other types, I've never seen before.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:55.080
Can you teach me what kind of slimes they are?

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:01.330
This is a scavenger slime.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.540
Scavenger slime.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:06.290
They eat trash and excrement.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:11.290
They can also deodorize,
and make fertilizer out of what they eat.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.450
I never knew such a slime exists!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.950
This is all news to me as well.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.580
Next, the cleaner slime.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.330
Their specialty is "cleansing."

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.040
Cleansing?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.160
I'll show you.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:28.410
This is a loincloth
taken from a goblin I defeated.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.500
What are you going to do with it?

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.000
Please watch.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:43.620
This always reminds me of a washing machine.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.830
It's completely spotless!

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:55.160
Unbelievable! Goblin grime is perhaps
the most difficult to clean in the world!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.160
It's so clean now!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:01.330
So, Mr. Ryoma, these slimes eat "grime"?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.700
Yes, that's what "cleansing" does.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:09.160
To be more accurate, they <i>only </i>eat grime, so...

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:10.700
Mr. Ryoma?!

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.080
I'm fine.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.540
You're not hurt?

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:20.120
Not only will it not harm humans,
it won't even eat animal meat, unless ordered.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.250
I've never heard of such a slime...

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.620
Well...

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.830
You scared us for a moment.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:28.330
Please don't startle us like that!

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:34.540
Um, I want a cleaner slime!

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:38.120
I will make the cleaner slime my first familiar!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.120
Oh, um...

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:44.830
I'd like to catch a slime that
will evolve into a cleaner slime!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.160
Please teach me how to pick it out!

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:51.870
Oh, um... It's hard to explain to a lady...

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.370
I see.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.700
I see how that could be hard
to discuss with the ladies.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:00.750
Indeed.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:03.620
I don't think women would want to
discuss this amongst themselves either.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.620
Right.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.620
Oh well. It is what it is.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.160
--What?!
--Hey, m'lady!

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.330
We figured it out!

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:13.750
What is it?!

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.330
Go wash up!

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:19.410
Then take the water with all your
sweat and filth in it and use it as bait!

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.660
He took the super direct approach!

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.790
It's incredible how tactless you are.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.540
Leave me alone.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:39.330
So... For some reason, slimes that can
potentially evolve into cleaner slimes

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:42.660
are attracted to water that contains sweat.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:47.080
I would never have guessed
that it would have such a trait...

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:48.250
I'm sorry.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:52.410
Oh, no, it's not your fault, Mr. Ryoma.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:57.700
I still want to find a cleaner slime.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.080
Maybe one of your guards can...

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:04.910
That's unacceptable.
I'm going to become a tamer.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.620
I can't rely on others.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.330
--Idiot!
--Doing everything by yourself
isn't always the best.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:12.910
--Doing everything by yourself
isn't always the best.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:17.660
Still, I want to take
the first step all by myself.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.870
It's your decision, my lady.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.790
I'll do it!

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.910
I'll catch it for sure!

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:35.450
I'm going now.

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:38.410
Good luck, my lady!

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:39.580
Have a safe trip.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:40.830
Yes!

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:48.910
I'm back!

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.370
This is my first familiar.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:56.330
I'll treasure him!

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:59.000
Congratulations.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:03.370
Wait, what did you say?

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:04.200
I said "Kamihiro."

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:05.750
I said "Tatsuo."

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:07.700
<i>Kamihiro</i>.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:08.540
<i>Tatsuo</i>.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.040
Starting now!

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.750
The very first familiar.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:33.290
I remember mine,
the sluggish but very precious...

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.290
...Tabuchi-kun.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:41.040
I named him after a younger coworker
because he reminded me of him.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.700
Although neither Tabuchi-kun is here now...

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.910
I hope he's happy in a new world somewhere.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.450
So...

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:54.120
Ryoma. Have you decided what to do from now on?

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:56.750
Oh, well...

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.040
To be honest, I can't decide.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:02.160
I could stay here, or move to a new place...

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.540
In that case, how's this?
Why don't you join us on our trip?

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:08.500
Trip?

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:14.000
We're traveling to a town named Gimul,
and will be staying there for a while.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:18.120
How does that sound? Of course,
you can return here at any time.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.000
What do you think?

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.120
A trip. A trip...

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:26.290
Leave the forest to go to a new world...?

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:29.290
When was the last time I took a trip...?

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:32.950
U-Um...

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:34.450
Mr. Ryoma.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:40.290
This is the first time I've taken a trip,
the first time I've been to this forest.

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.910
I was nervous when I left the town.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.700
No, I'm still nervous.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:49.950
But I saw so many new scenes,

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.580
met this precious friend,

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.790
and of course, met you, Mr. Ryoma.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:59.200
I'm sure there will be
hardships and sadness, too,

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:05.450
but I think there's much more fun
and joy to find in the outside world!

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:18.330
Thank you, my lady. I see...

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.040
The outside world must be...

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:28.870
I hate to cause trouble for you,
but may I join you?

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.250
Great! So you'll come!

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:32.790
I'm so glad!

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.580
Yes, I'm happy!

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:39.120
Good! In that case, we should
help you prepare for the trip.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:42.910
You can leave your belongings
with Sebas and his Item Box.

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:47.040
Oh, I can cast Item Box as well.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:47.870
What?!

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.120
You can cast Item Box?

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.330
Impressive!

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:52.910
Is it?

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:56.540
It is basic magic,
but it belongs to a higher element.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:59.870
Given your age, it is definitely impressive.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:01.290
I didn't know that...

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:05.910
Hey, if you want to learn more
about magic, you can ask me anything!

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:09.290
I'll teach you anything I know!

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:13.580
I'm going to enjoy studying with you, Mr. Ryoma!

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:19.330
I know little about this world.
I only have the knowledge the gods gave me.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:23.950
These people can teach me "common sense."

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.500
Thank you very much.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:28.290
I'm so glad I met them.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.500
That night...

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:37.500
...I stuffed everything in my house
into the Item Box.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:44.870
Fur from animals I hunted,
equipment from thieves I defeated...

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:48.790
I had built up quite a collection
over the past three years.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.660
I guess that'll do.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.000
To wrap up...

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.750
You must already know since you're gods,

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:04.410
but I'm going on my first journey in this world.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:08.910
I don't know when I can come back,
so I'll take everything I own with me.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:13.330
If I end up not coming back here,
I'll make another statue somewhere new.

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:17.620
The town, huh. I wonder what it's like.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:22.120
The next morning.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:29.290
It's now time to depart.

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.540
Locked and secured.

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:36.540
Ready to go?

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.200
The journey begins!

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:39.580
Yes!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:44.500
Yes, my first trip.
Let's take a step in a new direction.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:59.580
Mr. Sebas is incredible. He has
living animals in there, not just the cart.

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:03.330
Is that the intermediate
space magic, Dimension Home?

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:11.830
Mr. Ryoma. Is it true that you have
the Fire and Water elements,

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:15.040
in addition to Earth and Space?

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:18.620
Yes, my grandmother told me
I have all of the elements.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:19.620
Ah...

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:24.080
And you also use taming
and barrier magics, too, yes?

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:28.620
Those who have all the elements can end up
being a master of none. Be careful.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.410
I understand.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:34.160
Did I say something funny?

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.120
--Hmm?
--You were smiling a little.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:42.910
Ah, yes. I just remembered how
my grandmother told me the same thing.

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:47.040
I also tried my hand at healing magic
and alchemy as well, so.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:51.540
Alchemy? Now that's a rare one
to show interest in.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:54.080
Is alchemy uncommon?

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:57.080
You don't see it often nowadays.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:01.700
Alchemists can be very secretive,
and have a sinister image associated with them.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.200
What kind of alchemy did you work on, Mr. Ryoma?

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.660
The only thing I could pull off was

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:11.200
to remove mineral poisons
from rock salt to make it edible.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:14.040
That's quite impressive!

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.080
O-Oh, I see.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:19.450
It's like they shower me with
praise no matter what I do...

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:23.910
I really need to learn the
common-sense rules of this world soon.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:47.750
Looks like they're all happy, too.
I'm glad I took this trip.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:53.620
Over the next few days, we travelled by day,
and rested in tents at night.

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:56.120
It was quite a comfortable trip.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:11.250
It's quite uncommon to have
such heavy rain this time of year.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:13.700
It's a little cold...

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:17.160
Please, madam.

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.250
Thank you, Sebas.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:21.040
Are you all right, Elia?

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:23.120
Yes, I'm fine.

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.950
Thank you...

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:32.120
You're welcome.

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.830
Is something wrong?

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:35.370
Duke Reinhart!

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:36.580
We have a problem.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:45.040
It's completely blocked.
Is there another way around this?

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:49.040
It would be a huge detour--
perhaps three additional days.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.660
So much?

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:54.750
We've been told there are
thieves in these parts,

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:58.000
so we want to get through quickly.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:01.950
I see. I guess we have to
remove this with earth magic...

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:05.040
A landslide...

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:07.120
May I step outside for a moment?

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.700
Hmm? Well, of course, but...

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:11.700
What do you plan to do?

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:15.250
I think I can assist.

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.040
What's that?

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:19.620
It's a raincoat.

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:24.660
It's coated with the sticky solution
from a sticky slime, so it repels water.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:28.370
I was only aware of the adhesive
properties of that solution.

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:31.290
You're so full of surprises,
I thought I'd be used to this by now.

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:35.120
Yet here I am, still surprised.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.250
I'll go now.

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:41.870
P-Please be careful.

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:45.540
Do you think that cloak
has commercial potential?

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.950
That's a great idea!

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.500
Would Mr. Ryoma be able to profit from it?

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.950
Of course.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:57.120
When we get to town, let's introduce him
to Serge at the Morgan Trading Company.

00:19:57.120 --> 00:20:00.000
Use Break Rock to crush the large rocks,

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.160
and Rock to consolidate
the dirt into manageable sizes.

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:05.080
Understood.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.200
I guess there's no way around this.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:12.910
Envelop them and shield them
from the rain. Rain Block.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:16.580
The rain...

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:18.200
It's a barrier.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.040
Who cast this magic...?

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:22.660
It's you, Ryoma!

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:24.910
Thanks.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.870
You really are great.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:30.370
Thank you. And about that earth magic...

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.120
What is it?

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:35.620
Instead of casting Break Rock
and Rock separately,

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:40.950
you can use the combination magic based on
those two, Create Block, for efficiency.

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:43.750
"Create Block"?

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:48.370
It'll be easier to show you
than to explain verbally.

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.620
Create Block.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:05.120
Like this. Imagine casting the magic
on the rocks and dirt at the same time.

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:08.950
If you can cast Break Rock and Rock,
you should be able to do this, too.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:10.370
I see.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.450
Let's give it a shot!

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:13.040
In addition...

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:32.120
Now we can get through.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:36.910
I didn't expect it to go so quickly.
We can't thank you enough.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:43.160
You did so great, Ryoma!

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:44.620
You'll get mud on yourself!

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:46.580
I don't care about a little mud!

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:48.120
I... can't breathe...

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:49.660
Oh! I'm sorry.

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:51.160
I-It's fine...

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:56.000
That was exhausting, but I feel happy somehow.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:22:01.500
Being able to help
these people... It feels good.

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:06.620
For the next three days,
the journey went on without any trouble.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:07.870
Then...

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:11.500
That must be the mining town, Gimul.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:16.200
I've arrived at my very first town
since arriving in this world.
